</a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Explained Simply</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">What Does <span class="text-euro-600">SEDEX Stand For?</span></h2></div><p>Sedex stands for the <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">Supplier Ethical Data Exchange</strong>, a global online platform that lets buyers and suppliers share ethical trade data in one place. It is a membership organisation, not an audit body and not a certification scheme.</p><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Explained Simply</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">What Does <span class="text-euro-600">SMETA Stand For?</span></h2></div><p>SMETA stands for the <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">Sedex Members Ethical Trade Audit</strong>, the audit methodology created by Sedex members to check working conditions in supply chains. SMETA is the most widely used social audit format in the world. Eurocert conducts SMETA audits as an approved auditing company, and the finished report is uploaded to the Sedex platform where your buyer can review it.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Not The Same Thing</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">SEDEX <span class="text-euro-600">vs SMETA</span></h2></div><p>Sedex is the data exchange and membership platform. SMETA is the audit standard used to inspect a supplier's site and produce an agreed report format. A useful way to remember the difference: <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">you register on Sedex, but an approved auditor conducts SMETA.</strong> Sedex itself does not issue certificates, and neither does SMETA - the deliverable is the audit report shared on the platform.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Scope Options</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">2-Pillar <span class="text-euro-600">vs 4-Pillar SMETA</span></h2></div><p>A 2-pillar SMETA assesses <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">labour standards</strong> and <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">health and safety</strong>. A 4-pillar SMETA adds <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">environment</strong> and <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-700">business ethics</strong> sections. Most UK and European retailers require the 4-pillar version, while some buyers accept 2-pillar for lower-risk categories. Your buyer's requirements usually decide the scope.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Planning</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">Cost &amp; <span class="text-euro-600">Duration</span></h2></div><p>A SMETA audit cost depends on site size, number of workplaces, whether you choose 2-pillar or 4-pillar, and its location. As a guide, single-site facilities typically budget in the range of GBP 1,500 to 4,000 including report production and Sedex upload. The audit itself usually takes one to three days on site, and the full process - from booking to a completed report on the Sedex platform - normally sits between two and four weeks.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Before The Audit</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">What Is the <span class="text-euro-600">SEDEX SAQ?</span></h2></div><p>The SAQ (Self-Assessment Questionnaire) is the online form you complete in your Sedex account covering labour standards, health and safety, environment and business ethics. Completing the SAQ before the audit improves data quality and shortens audit time. Auditors can also start the SMETA report from your SAQ answers.</p><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">The Result</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">SMETA Report <span class="text-euro-600">and CAPR</span></h2></div><p>After the audit you receive the SMETA audit report plus a Corrective Action Plan Report (CAPR) listing non-conformances and agreed action points. The CAPR stays in your Sedex account so you can track closure with your buyer. Helping you prepare is part of our service - we share a pre-audit checklist covering records, workers, interviews and site walkthrough, so your team is ready on the day.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Related Audits</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">Other Social <span class="text-euro-600">Audit Programmes</span></h2></div><p>Buyers increasingly ask for additional ethical trade schemes alongside or instead of SMETA. Eurocert offers <a href="/social-audits/sa-8000/" class="text-euro-600 font-semibold hover:underline">SA8000 certification</a>, <a href="/social-audits/code-of-conduct/" class="text-euro-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Code of Conduct audits</a>, <a href="/social-audits/slcp/" class="text-euro-600 font-semibold hover:underline">SLCP (Social &amp; Labor Convergence Program)</a> assessments, <a href="/social-audits/ctpat/" class="text-euro-600 font-semibold hover:underline">C-TPAT</a> and WRAP. Tell us which scheme your buyer requires and we will scope the audit accordingly, combining assessments where the standards allow.</p></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white border-t border-slate-100"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">FAQ</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">SMETA / Sedex <span class="text-euro-600">FAQ</span></h2></div><details class="seo-faq"><summary>Is SEDEX a certification?</summary><div class="ans">No. Sedex is a data-sharing platform and SMETA is an audit methodology. The output of a SMETA audit is a report uploaded to Sedex, not a certificate.</div></details><details class="seo-faq"><summary>Which pillar do I need?</summary><div class="ans">Check your buyer's request. 4-pillar (labour, H&amp;S, environment, business ethics) is the common retail default; 2-pillar is acceptable in some categories.</div></details><details class="seo-faq"><summary>How long is a SMETA report valid?</summary><div class="ans">Buyers often expect a new SMETA audit every 12 months, though some accept 24 months. Follow your buyer's validation requirements.</div></details><details class="seo-faq"><summary>Do you cover multiple sites in one audit?</summary><div class="ans">Yes. Multi-site and multi-workplace facilities can be assessed and reported in a single SMETA audit, with the scope clearly defined in the report.</div></details><details class="seo-faq"><summary>Does Eurocert help with the Sedex registration?</summary><div class="ans">We guide you through platform registration and SAQ completion as part of the audit engagement, but registration and membership remain your responsibility as the Sedex member.</div></details></div></div></section><style is:global>.seo-faq{border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:12px;background:#f8fafc;margin-bottom:10px;overflow:hidden}.seo-faq summary{cursor:pointer;padding:16px 20px;font-weight:700;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;color:#0f172a}.seo-faq summary::after{content:"+";color:#1d4ed8;font-weight:800}.seo-faq .ans{padding:0 20px 16px;color:#64748b;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7}</style>
</BaseLayout>
